  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This problem has the exact same setup as qUiRkY qUesTs (Easy). The only difference between them is that in this version, you must solve the problem for every prefix of the given array.**\n\nSuppose you have an array BBB. Consider performing the following operation on it:\n\n\nFirst, choose any non-empty subsequence of BBB.\nThen, replace each element of this subsequence with the MEX†^\\dagger† of BBB.\n\nNote that while you choose a subsequence, the replacement is done with the MEX of the entire array BBB, not only the elements of the subsequence.\n\n\nFor example, if B=[1,0,4,1,2]B = [1, 0, 4, 1, 2]B=[1,0,4,1,2] and you choose the subsequence [1,0,1][1, 0, 1][1,0,1], those elements will be replaced by the MEX of BBB (which equals 333), to obtain [3,3,4,3,2][3, 3, 4, 3, 2][3,3,4,3,2].\n\nWe define f(B)f(B)f(B) to be the **maximum** possible sum of BBB that can be obtained by performing the given operation any number of times (possibly, zero).\n\nNote that since BBB is changed after a move, its MEX may also change for future moves.\n\nNow, for the actual problem.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nFor each i∈[1,N]i \\in [1, N]i∈[1,N], compute f([A1,A2,…,Ai])f([A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i])f([A1​,A2​,…,Ai​]).\n\nThis is, solve the problem for each prefix of AAA.\n\n†^\\dagger† The MEX (minimum excludant) of an array of integers is defined as the smallest non-negative integer which does not occur in the array. For example:\n\n\nThe MEX of [2,2,1][2,2,1][2,2,1] is 000 because 000 is not in the array.\nThe MEX of [0,1,2][0,1,2][0,1,2] is 333 because 0,1,20, 1, 20,1,2 are present in the array but 333 is not.\nThe MEX of [3,0,1][3,0,1][3,0,1] is 222 because 0,10, 10,1 are present in the array but 222 is not.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output NNN space-separated integers, where the ithi^{th}ith integer denotes the value of f([A1,A2,…,Ai])f([A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i])f([A1​,A2​,…,Ai​]).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2×1051 \\leq T \\leq 2 \\times 10^51≤T≤2×105",
      "1≤N≤2×1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\times 10^51≤N≤2×105",
      "0≤Ai≤10120 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^{12} 0≤Ai​≤1012 for all 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2×1052 \\times 10^52×105."
    ],
